e?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110519 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "333792dd-67b0-5673-821a-304ad5011c62" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110519 #edb/ref 1074 "The volume $V$ of a cube can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nV = s^3\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the side length of the cube.\n\nSubstituting\n\n$$\ns=4\\,\\textrm{cm}\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we get\n\n$$\nV = (4\\, \\textrm{cm})^3 = 64\\, \\textrm{cm}^3\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110520 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7178" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110520 #edb/ref 1071 "The volume of a cube is $729\\, \\textrm{cm}^3$. Find the length of the edges of the cube." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110520 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0d03e2bd-c8a2-5a16-a5b2-b51dbf9e408a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110520 #edb/ref 1074 "Since the volume of a cube is\n\n$$\nV = s^3\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the length of an edge, we can find $s$ as follows:\n\n$$\ns = \\sqrt[3]{V} = \\sqrt[3]{729} = 9\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of the edges is $9\\,\\textrm{cm}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110539 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8977" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110539 #edb/ref 1071 "Six identical plastic cubic containers have a combined volume of $48 \\: \\textrm{ft}^3$. Find the side length of a single container." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110539 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f265fcf1-8d50-5908-8df4-6df66cb0673a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110539 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the volume of a single container:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{48 \\: \\textrm{ft}^3}{6} = 8 \\: \\textrm{ft}^3\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the side length of one container.\n\nSince the volume of a cube is\n\n$$\nV = s^3\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the length of a side, we can find $s$ as follows:\n\n$$\ns = \\sqrt[3]{V} = \\sqrt[3]{8} = 2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of a side of a single container is $2\\,\\textrm{ft}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110644 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186051057 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110644 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186110884 