45417] [17592186111583 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110655 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111891 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose that we have a cube whose edges are $2\\,\\textrm{cm}$ in length, like the one shown below.\n\n![](images/b9/b974b6e782801fbe2099971afd0df9a5c6e05a10afc2ce0e4054c850088e753b.png)\n\nThe formula for the volume $V$ of a cube with sides of length $s$ is given by\n\n$$\nV = s^3\n$$\n\nTo find the volume of this cube, we substitute\n\n$$\ns=2 \\: \\textrm{cm}\n$$\n\ninto the formula. This gives\n\n$$\nV = (2\\, \\textrm{cm})^3 = 8 \\text{cm}^3\n$$\n\nSo the volume of the cube is $8\\,\\textrm{cm}^3$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111891 #edb/ref 1065 4348 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111891 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "7ebfe2f1-6dce-5f67-bf2d-58fcd1660014" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111891 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
